  "body": "Stacked on #941 (base `issue/916-solidcore-step-bench`; retarget to `main` before #941 merges).\n\n## What changed (crates/kernel only)\n- `machining_mesh::machining_mesh(&StepSolid, tol_mm, &CancelToken)`: meshes the solid's reader record with solidcore-tess at `MeshTolerance::chord(tol_mm)` and returns a `MachiningMesh` (welded positions in mm, triangles, face per triangle, `MeshReport`) or a named `MeshRefusal`. Refused: a tolerance not finite/positive or under a millionth of the body (tess would coarsen it silently); `unmeshed`, `lenient`, `unsampled_edges`, `over_tolerance`/`edges_capped` with `within == false`, any evaluator refusal, a face with no triangles; more than 30 M triangles (the app's `MAX_FACETS`); an unmeasurable triangle; a judged deviation past the tolerance; an open, over-shared or turned side after an exact-position weld; a non-positive volume; a panic in the mesher; the time bound. Notes only: capped-but-within faces/edges, `kept_strict`, `averaged_poles`.\n- `mesh_deviation`: 15 barycentric samples a triangle; parametric |S(u,v)-T(u,v)| against the plan surface, and the closed-form distance to the record face's analytic surface (plane, cylinder, cone, sphere, torus, ball patch). Judged by the analytic distance where the face is analytic, else parametric (the parametric one over-reads a rational circle by a few per cent: 5.058e-3 vs a true 4.965e-3 on Milling-test).\n- `StepSolid` keeps its `record`. solidcore-tess moves from dev- to library dependency; solidcore-record named directly (both already locked, same rev; no new package).\n\n## Readings (release; decision file has the full table)\n| File | tol | sc-tess tris / judged | truck tris / common measure |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Milling-test (mm and inch) | 0.005 | 6228 (6248 inch) / 4.97e-3 | 952 / 4.95e-3 (open mesh) |\n| sample_ap214 (metre) | 0.005 | 11894 / 4.95e-3 | 3178 / **9.99e-3** (truck's 0.01 floor) |\n| sample_ap214 | 0.01 | 7920 / 9.86e-3 | 3178 / 9.99e-3 |\n| box, empty_list, tool box | both | 12 / 0 | 12 / 0 |\n\nwasm32: `cargo check -p camcraft-kernel --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` passes; no rayon in the wasm32 tree.\n\n## How tested\n- Default lane (`tests/machining_mesh.rs`): `machining_mesh_is_watertight_and_within_tolerance`, `a_bad_tolerance_or_a_spent_time_bound_is_refused_by_name`, `every_planner_shortfall_is_a_refusal_or_a_note`, `the_deviation_measure_sees_a_moved_node_and_a_wrong_surface`, `analytic_distances_are_the_closed_forms`.\n- Kernel release lane (`#[ignore]`): `machining_mesh_deviation_bench` (every fixture at 0.005 and 0.01 mm, verdicts pinned, 1.4 s).\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-kernel` (all green) and `-- --ignored` (all green), `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`, wasm32 check.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No fixture provokes a real planner shortfall (checked down to 1e-4 mm); the decisions are pinned on synthetic `PlanStats` -> #1029.\n- Deviation is sampled, not proven; spline/revolved faces only get the parametric reading (none on the fixtures) -> #1029.\n- solidcore-tess `plan` has no cancel hook; it runs to its end inside its memory bounds.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` not run: the Cargo.lock change falls it back to batch (all of app/ui, no kernel suite), as on #941; the kernel suites above were run instead.\n\nChangelog: kernel seam: a machining mesh of a solidcore STEP solid from solidcore-tess, watertight and measured within its chord tolerance, every mesher shortfall a named refusal (bench only; the app still meshes through truck)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #940\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
